      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:95:2",
      "text": [
        " لَا يَحْتَجِمِ الْمُحْرِمُ إِلَّا أَنْ يَخَافَ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ أَنْ لَا يَسْتَطِيعَ الصَّلَاةَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Musna Bin Abdul Salaam, from Zurara, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> cannot get cupping done unless if he fears upon himself, or unable to Pray’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Hassan ibn Ali from Muthanna’ ibn ‘Abd al-Salam from Zurarah who has said the following: “Abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘One in the state of Ihram, must not use cupping (draw blood from one’s body) unless one fears for his life and that one cannot perform Salat (prayer).”’ "
        ]
      }
